terminal-system — AI-assisted two-pane terminal
================================================

Usage: terminal-system [claude|codex]

Opens a tmux session with two panes:

  - Left pane: a normal shell. This is where commands actually run.
  - Right pane: type instructions in natural language, e.g.
    "crea utente Pippo". The chosen AI engine translates the
    instruction into shell command(s), which are typed into the left
    pane in real time.

Right-pane commands:
  :auto on|off            toggle automatic execution (default: off)
  :engine claude|codex    switch AI engine for the rest of the session
  :quit                   end the session

Confirmation:
  By default every generated command waits for you to press Enter (or
  type "n" to cancel it) before it runs. With ":auto on", safe commands
  run automatically — but a fixed set of dangerous patterns (rm -rf /,
  mkfs, dd onto /dev, fork bombs, chmod -R 777 /, shutdown/reboot,
  killall -9, userdel/groupdel on root/sudo/admin, iptables -F, writing
  onto /dev/sdX) always stops for manual confirmation regardless of
  auto-mode.

Session memory:
  Instructions, generated commands, and recent left-pane output are
  kept as context for the rest of the session (so "ora aggiungilo al
  gruppo sudo" can refer back to a user you just created), but nothing
  is written to disk — history disappears when the session ends.

Requires:
  The claude and/or codex CLI already installed and authenticated.
  Neither is a hard package dependency.
